<title>MOROCCO: Morocco lifts control on banana imports.</title>
<headline>Morocco lifts control on banana imports.</headline>
<dateline>RABAT 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morocco lifted controls on banana imports effective May 13, 1997, the state-run Office des Changes said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The regulatory office said in a circular local importers could submit import demands directly to intermediary banks. They would no longer require prior permission for banana imports.</p>
<p>Last November, Morocco imposed controls which made it compulsory for banks to submit a prior demand for banana imports. The move was aimed at protecting local farmers from imports from Costa Rica and Caribbean countries.</p>
<p>Morocco has gradually liberalised commodity imports, including fruit, since May 1996. The average banana price on the domestic market is 12 dirhams ($1.4) per kg.</p>
<p>($1= 9.3 dirhams)</p>
<p>--Rabat newsroom (212-7 72 65 18)</p>
